            <ArticleTitle>Comprehensive evaluation of a patient with Kawasaki disease and giant coronary aneurysms with cardiac magnetic resonance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E195-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/chd.12131</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with Kawasaki disease (KD) and coronary artery aneurysms (CAAs), serial evaluation with multiple imaging modalities is recommended to guide risk stratification and management. We present the case of a 7-year-old boy with a history of KD and multiple giant CAAs who developed thrombosis in one of the aneurysms. We illustrate how cardiac magnetic resonance is unique in allowing a comprehensive assessment in patients with severe KD and how it may affect their management.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2013 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
